{"id": "section-body-04581", "title": "Lymphatic Filariasis", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "blocks": [{"id": "body-04581", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Lymphatic Filariasis", "runs": [{"text": "Lymphatic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Filariasis"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1751"}}, {"id": "body-04582", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Lymphatic filariasis is a parasitic disease caused by thread-like filarial worms (Wuchereria bancrofti, Brugia malayi, and Brugia timori) transmitted through mosquito bites. The parasites lodge in the lymphatic system, causing damage that leads to abnormal enlargement of body parts and disability.", "runs": [{"text": "Lymphatic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "filariasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parasitic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "thread-like"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "filarial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "worms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "("}, {"text": "Wuchereria", "italic": true}, {"text": " ", "italic": true}, {"text": "bancrofti", "italic": true}, {"text": ","}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Brugia", "italic": true}, {"text": " ", "italic": true}, {"text": "malayi", "italic": true}, {"text": ","}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Brugia timori", "italic": true}, {"text": ") transmitted through mosquito bites. The parasites lodge in the lymphatic system, causing damage that leads to abnormal enlargement of body parts and disability."}]}, {"id": "body-04584", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04585", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Acute episodes of fever with painful swelling of lymph nodes, typically in the groin or armpit", "runs": [